**RIVER + ORGANIC TOWN (2026-10-05, live, world file `river 2026-10-05`, backup `pre_river 2026-10-05`, 3,165,239 bricks):** owner: big long river, bridges over water on paths, spawn town "less square, connected by herringbone paths", hamlets laid out like RuneScape's map.
- mapgen `RIVER` (rw 3+K, bank 12, depth 2): course = waypoints down the island (spineAt, side clear of dungeons) -> town `RIVER_LOCAL` -> out west to the sea; level only falls, pinned to town.h-1 in town, levees where ground is low; glass water (collision off) bed->level where level > SEA; `riverCell/riverLevel/keepOut/noSmooth` arrays gate trees/plants/caves/outposts/smoothing; villages + swamp avoid it.
- Bridges: mapgen roads over water (river or H <= SEA) -> plank deck per cell (micro, top = level+2 / SEA+2) + rails on open-water edges; town paths over the river -> stone decks + parapets (town.mjs `bridges()`).
- town.mjs: `planTown(rnd)` (paths: 4 exits + castle + church spurs + up to 16 fanned lanes, plaza r 360, ragged-disc edge `edgeR`) is computed in mapgen before flattening; `surface(ux, uy, plan)` -> 'square' | 'street' (herringbone) | 'lot' | null (natural ground). Only plan cells flatten (BFS blend); no wall, no grid. `build({plan, riverAt})`: plaza fountain/spawns, castle, church(+graveyard), bank, tavern fixed; `housesAlong()` puts houses facing the paths (footprint/rectClear checks), `lampsAlong()`, trees. Hamlets: `planVillage(seed)` (green + 3-4 herringbone spokes to VILLAGE_R 880), houses along spokes, fenced fields + a pen; roads join the nearest spoke end. TOWN_DEBUG=1 records rejected sites in stats.rejectAt.

