## Server
- `ssh pzedlo.hopto.org` (user max). Node: `~/node22/bin/node`. Omegga in `~/omegga-server`, log `/tmp/omegga_pty2.log` (filter out `LogBRRemoteBundle` spam).
- Bridge job: `node ~/omegga-server/bridge/tools/job.mjs < job.json` (gives up after 60 s; for long jobs drop the file into `bridge/inbox/<id>` (write `.tmp`, then mv) and poll `bridge/outbox/<id>`).
  Ops: `players`, `cmd {line, captureMs}`, `bricks {at:[0,0,0], bricks, owner?, captureMs}`, `say {msg}`, `sleep {ms}`, `clear`, `emit`.
- Every map/dungeon upload goes in ONE `bricks` op, preceded by `say` `<size="40"><color="ff4040"><b>"I DONT CARE IF THE FUCKIN SERVER CRASHES JUST DO IT ALL AT ONCE"</></></>`.
- GAME MODE TRAP (2026-10-06): a world file created by SaveAs gets the default Sandbox game mode (weapon damage OFF: nobody can melee). The live world `world 2026-10-06 combat` has the old Blank game mode patched in (GameMode/GameMode/Settings.json, GameMode/Rules/GameMode.json, GameMode/Teams/Unaffiliated.json + Manifest copied from `pre_regen 2026-10-05.brdb` via sqlite: keep inventory, persistent checkpoints, enhanced brickadians, friendly damage, ConsiderTeamHostile "New Team"). Redeploy INTO it (Bricks.Clear + load + `br.World.Save`), never SaveAs. Henge moved next to spawn 2026-10-06 (spineAt(0.05, -45K), live ~(-3540, 6420)); backup by cp: `backup pre_henge 2026-10-06.brdb`.
- BACKUP TRAP (2026-10-06): `br.World.SaveAs "name"` makes "name" the ACTIVE world, so the 5-minute autosave keeps writing into it; SaveAs to an existing name fails (AlreadyExists). A "backup" taken with SaveAs before a wipe gets overwritten by the wiped/half-loaded world (pre_gen / pre_gen2 2026-10-05 are empty). Back up by copying the active .brdb on disk (`cp "data/Saved/Worlds/<active>.brdb" "data/Saved/Worlds/<backup>.brdb"` after a save), and SaveAs only to a NEW name once the new world is loaded. Active world now: `world 2026-10-06` (scale 2).
- BMX PATHS (2026-10-06, owner: "ensure that the paths are bmx compatible"): `mapgen/bmxcheck.mjs P.bin OUT` samples the riding surface every stud on every path cell (preview flag 128 = pathCell | villagePaved | townKind 2; preview section `ride` = deck top / tunnel floor / ground / town paving on town bridges), wedge + corner pieces modelled as slopes (outer corner = min(1, t1+t2), triangle cap = max(0, t1+t2-1), MicroWedgeCorner = min), poles and <=10-thin pieces (rails, parapets) are obstacles not surface, 20-unit headroom; reports LIPs (a jump between two flat tops) vs steep ramps; writes OUT/bmx_steps.json. Fixes: straight roads (gate leads, no-route fallbacks) are now graded (they rode the raw ground), bridge decks get a plank wedge ramp (between the rails) up to a higher road cell. Lips 108 -> 36 (road corridor overlaps on bends ~10 spots, one tunnel portal at live ~3300,180). ~28k steep-ramp samples are 2-3 brick smoothing wedges, mostly across the road corridor. Backup mapgen.mjs.pre_bmx.
- DORMERS (2026-10-06, owner's picture, LIVE as a delta 411/495): roofs.mjs `ROOF_POOL` [gable 0.6, dormer 0.4] + `pickRoof`, town.mjs shapedSpec picks `roof` per house (rnd(s, 91)). shapedhouse `roof: 'dormer'` = gable profile + 1 (W < 40) or 2 dormers (W/3, 2W/3) on the front (-y) slope: bands kf (30% up) .. kb-1 cut over a 6-stud width, cheek walls per cut band, board floor, sill/jambs/glass/head front, a lip+wedge roof each side (ridge front-to-back, 1 stud past the front), a back wall up to band kb; walls 3 courses (2 on low roofs); 32x20 cottages get none. `dormers` count in the shapedHouse result. Backups *.pre_dormer, mapgen/out_pre_dormer1006.
- GABLES (2026-10-06 16:35, owner: "roofs have several issues", LIVE as an exact delta: 17,057 clears / 17,699 adds, 0 rejects): shapedhouse `shade()` = one factor per brick for all channels (was per channel: pink/yellow/blue speckled gables); town `gable(..., fill)` lays the gable end as 12-high running-bond micro bricks (20-60 long) instead of one flat slab per roof course. `stats.gables` records every gable box (elevation checks). Backups shapedhouse.mjs.pre_gablefix, town.mjs.pre_gablefix2, mapgen/out_pre_roof1006.
- REGEN 2026-10-06 16:20 (owner: "generate"): LIVE now = organic hamlets + river valley + flatter swamp/desert + bows + bank-safe market (1,491,862 bricks, 6 overlap rejects; 104 spawners (8 needed z+12..36), 61 stands, XP chip, sea preset). Active world `world 2026-10-06 live` (backup by cp: `backup pre_regen 2026-10-06.brdb`); mapgen/out = live (old out_pre_regen1006), server bridge/map_live = live (old map_live_pre_regen1006).
- WIPE HOW-TO: there is NO Bricks.ClearAll (neither prefix). `br.Bricks.Clear <ownerId> 1` per owner (map = owner 891c4675...; list owners from the .brdb), then `br.World.ClearRegion 0 0 0 60000 60000 30000` on the empty map clears the prefab entities (chips/stands/spawners). A .brdb keeps stale entity-grid rows after clears; trust the game's "No bricks to clear".
- STARTUP WORLD TRAP (2026-10-06): server restarts at 14:57/15:04 came up on `backup pre_henge 2026-10-06` (6 MB, no map) and autosaved into it; the startup world setting wasn't found in Config/omegga-config. After any restart check the log for which .brdb opened and `br.World.Load "world 2026-10-06 live"` if wrong.
- BOT CAP (2026-10-06, owner): the server allows only 300 bots at once (in-game Bot Limit). Every spawner prefab is one B_Bot_Spawn_Point = one bot; keep spawners.json + extras well under 300 (105 live). Outpost spawners often get rejected ('Brick is overlapping in same grid'): re-place at z+12/+24.
- ORDERING TRAP: console `cmd` ops queue in the game and run at ~100/s, but the `bricks` op loads immediately. A job with thousands of ClearRegions followed by a bricks load ends up clearing the NEW bricks. Clear in one job, wait until the log shows the clears done, then load in a second job (or only clear when the count is small).
- `br.World.ClearRegion cx cy cz hx hy hz` removes only bricks ENTIRELY inside; logs `Cleared N bricks`.
- Read bricks from the world: `br.Prefab.SaveRegion "name" cx cy cz hx hy hz 0` → `data/Saved/Prefabs/name.brz`; parse with `brs.WorldReader.from(bytes)` from `plugins/bridge/lib/brs.mjs`; `r.bricks(gridId)`, `r.brickAssets()[b.asset_name_index]`, `r.brickOwners()[b.owner_index - 1]` (owner index is 1-based; 0 = ours/none). Reading a `.brdb`: `new brs.Brdb(new (await import('node:sqlite')).DatabaseSync(file, {readOnly:true}))`, then wrap `r.bricks(g)` per grid in try (some entity grids throw).
- Player position: `players` op. Teleport: `br.Chat.Command /TP "name" x y z 0` (plain Chat.Command is not recognized). Kill: `br.Server.Players.Kill "name"`. Spawner prefabs: `br.Prefab.Load "dungeon_spawner_<tier>" x y z 0 16`.

## Units & geometry (verified in-game)
- 1 stud = 10 units, brick height 12, plate 4. Sizes are HALF extents. Procedural x/y half-extents multiple of 5, z multiple of 2, or the game says "Missing brick type". Micro bricks snap to 2.
- Orientation code = direction*4 + rotation; `mapgen/orient.mjs` ORIENT[] maps local→world axes. Direction 4 = Z+ (upright). Rotation r (about +Z) = r quarter turns anticlockwise: local (x,y) → r1 (-y,x), r2 (-x,-y), r3 (y,-x).
- `PB_DefaultRampCorner` / `PB_DefaultRampCornerInverted`, direction 4: rotation 0 slopes down toward (+x,+y), 1 → (-x,+y), 2 → (-x,-y), 3 → (+x,-y). Used for the owner's pillar flares (`flare()` in dungeon.mjs).
- `PB_DefaultMicroWedge` is natively a SIDE wedge; use `orientFor()`. Local size must be permuted with the orientation or the AABB overlaps and the brick is rejected.
- The game rejects overlapping bricks: everything goes through `mapgen/builder.mjs` (`box/slab/pole/add`), which drops overlaps; generators throw if anything is dropped.

## Map (mapgen/)
- FLATTER SWAMP + DESERT (2026-10-06, owner: "more natural looking and flatter geometry"; generator only, NOT live): swamp = oval (x1.3 along a seed angle) with a ragged lobed edge (`swampRho`), grass hummock islands (fbm > 0.22, not swampCell), blend 28, and a `swamp.basin` 45-cell low basin round it (only lowers). Desert site + `desertW` moved BEFORE the hamlets and levelled: mean height + swells (9) + wind dunes (4) + rare buttes (10-16), guarded off river (cut only), dungeon hills, town. Backup mapgen.mjs.pre_flatbiomes.
- RIVER VALLEY (2026-10-06, owner: the river ran in a sheer canyon, "make this look natural"; generator only, NOT live): mapgen `valleyRise(e)` cuts the ground (never fills) to level+1 + 1 brick/cell for 4 cells, steepening to `river.slope` 4.5/cell by the bank's end, out to `river.valley` 40 cells past the banks, roughened with fbm (6 voxels). Steps > 20 bricks within 50 cells of the river: 1593 -> 42. Backup mapgen.mjs.pre_valley.
- ORGANIC HAMLETS (2026-10-06, owner: hamlets were circles, wanted varied/organic; generator only, NOT live yet): town.mjs `planVillage` = lumpy outline `edgeR` (0.92 VILLAGE_R + sine lobes, 620..840), 3-4 lanes spread round with +-0.45 rad jitter, bends/wiggle, irregular green; houses every 100 along lanes (side lanes tried: halved the houses). mapgen levels ONLY the footprint (paved cells + every `st.taken` plot from a trial build of each hamlet, desert and green variants) with a chamfer distance `v.used`; `villageDist` = that distance + VILLAGE.r (inside = VILLAGE.r - 2), so all exclusions/smoothing follow the footprint. ~2.9 houses/hamlet (was 3.4). Backups town.mjs.pre_organic / mapgen.mjs.pre_organic.
- BOWS (2026-10-06, owner's 6 hand-placed bows at live ~(-5..95,-355,582), PickupClass 64): server `bridge/tools/bowshopgen.mjs` -> `bow_<bow|oak|willow|maple|yew|magic>.brz` (owner's names/damage/speed/colours exactly; price 50/400/1000/4000/8000/20000). town.mjs market wares now 27 + 6 bows = 33; stands are placed AFTER the bank via `free()` (builder.free, passed from mapgen) so no spot lands on a column (the bank portico ate the oak spot). Live: placed by hand at (-380,-120) (-400,-30) (-330,220) (-310,250) (-280,290) (-250,320) z 588, = next generator output; bridge/map_live/shops.json updated (old: shops.pre_bows.json). Bought bows are not in the XP chip's SwordTier give-back.
- WORLDGEN EDITOR (2026-10-06): `node mapgen/editor/server.mjs` -> http://localhost:8787. mapgen `tune(key, def, note)` tunables (terrain.*, island.spine/half, sea, crypt/keep/deep/henge .t/.off, river, swamp, village, outposts, desert, caves, dungeon.*, smooth.maxRise) overridden by `--params FILE` (flat {key: value} or an editor preset {seed, scale, params}); defaults = byte-identical live output (checked, 317 files). Previews: `--preview F --preview-height` (~3 s), `--preview F` (sites, ~20 s), `--preview F --preview-full` (all bricks rasterised, ~55 s); format in preview.mjs. Presets in editor/presets, cache in editor/cache, Build writes mapgen/out_<name> (never out/, never deploys). Add a new tunable by wrapping its constant in tune(); put it in HEIGHT_KEYS in index.html if it changes the bare heightmap. Caves are now checked lazily against a pre-facade height copy (same picks, 34 -> 22 s).
- `node mapgen.mjs --seed 786559213 --out DIR [--dry]` (live seed). Writes `chunk_*.json`, `spawners.json`, `town_removed.json`, and a JSON summary to stderr (town centre, dungeon centres/entrances).
