## !ai builder (chatbot plugin)
Local source: `omegga-chatbot/` (`omegga.main.js` → server `plugins/chatbot/`, `shapes.js` → `plugins/chatbot/lib/`). Deploy with scp, then `node ~/omegga-server/bridge/tools/reload.mjs`.
- Parts are painted into a stud × stud × plate voxel grid (later parts win, `carve` erases), then greedily merged into bricks, so builds have no overlap losses.
- Text-friendly parts: `extrude` (ASCII side view), `layers` (voxels), `revolve`, `cylinder`, `line`.
- The build result returns ASCII FRONT/SIDE/TOP previews plus WARNING lines (parts that made nothing, floating pieces); chat shows only the first line.
- The model runs through the FCC proxy (the model mapping lives in its env; don't read it). Rounds take ~70-110 s.
- Tickets: every !ai/!agent/!img takes a numbered ticket (store `ticketNo`, `tickets`); up to max-parallel run, the rest queue. Chat lines are tagged [AI][#n] via AsyncLocalStorage (this.current); thinking lines use size thinking-size (11). Commands: !ticket !tickets !cancel !rate 1-5 [#] !ratings, /help (+ /aihelp; `!help` is Omegga's own).
- Welcome message: `data/Saved/Config/LinuxServer/GameUserSettings.ini` `WelcomeMessage` (Crimpo Quest wishlist link, Steam app 4192470, tracked with ?utm_source=brick); read at server start.
- Test as a player with the bridge op `{op:'emit', event:'chatcmd:ai', args:['soapstain22', ...words]}`.

## Media plugin (/playvideo, /playaudio)
Local `omegga-media/` -> server `plugins/media/` (scp + reload; config via `bridge/tools/rpc.mjs plugin.config media '<full json>'`). Video pixels 2 units (1 micro brick); detailed cells use the owner's 4-segment (4x PB_DefaultMicroWedgeHalfInnerCornerInverted at one spot: on a -x screen top 3/1, right(+y) 4/2, bottom 4/0, left 5/0) or 2-ramp diagonal cells (PB_DefaultMicroRamp 4/3+5/1 or 4/1+5/3); overlapping pieces load fine. Audio default `layered`: bass <250 Hz triangle voices, mids sine voices, highs bank with pink/white noise bands (voice mode ignores --noise-bands/--release; bank mode only spans notes around A440). Tuning loop (2026-10-05): the game runs on this PC, so `scratchpad`-style scripts record WASAPI loopback (pip pyaudiowpatch) while auto-started probe devices play at the owner, then compare octave levels/envelopes with the source (score 0.61 -> 0.74; mids 32 voices, --voice-release 15). Game synth at 440 Hz measured: square ~1.38x sine RMS, triangle ~0.81x.

- Media fixes 2026-10-06 (owner: busted, "static and really high pitched notes"): (1) speakers were refused with "Failed to attach component, reason: 2" because the patched world Settings had Limits {} -> restored `MaxActiveComponents` 500000 (+ MaxPendingCustomEventsPerGate 79, bEnforceApplicatorLimits) via /tmp/limits.mjs (brs Brdb.mergeFolder on a copy) and `br.World.Load "world 2026-10-06 live"` (active world now); any world-file patch must keep these limits. (2) layered devices were 20 apart but ~35 wide, so each pre-load ClearRegion ate the previous device: `deviceStep()` spaces by real width. (3) highs layer (noise + square bank, droned ~1760 Hz) dropped; mids capped at 2 kHz; bass gain 1.5. (4) music.youtube.com links rewritten to www. Verified by loopback recording (scratchpad listen.py): video note match 0.29 -> ~0.8, no hiss/drone.

## !tpa plugin
Local `omegga-tpa/` → server `plugins/tpa/` (scp, then `bridge/tools/reload.mjs`). !tpa/!tpahere <partial name>, !tpaccept|!tpyes / !tpdeny|!tpno [name], !tpcancel; 60 s expiry, 5 s cooldown (config). Moves with `br.Chat.Command /TP "name" x y z 0` to the other player's position +10 z.

## Style rules (owner's taste)
Zelda caves (doorway → single room), not Minecraft tunnels. Caves (mapgen `CAVE`/`cellsOf`, 2026-10-03 "more intricate"): irregular blob room up to 9 cells, domed ceiling 9-14 voxels, raised back ledge, side alcoves, rock pillar, stalactites/stalagmites/glow crystals, fires + old man/chest on the ledge. Smooth terrain with micro wedges, not stair steps. No stud/underside textures: regular bricks have an ugly bottom, so anything whose underside can show (ceilings, lintels, roof crowns, overhangs) is `PB_DefaultMicroBrick` or `PB_DefaultTile`; shapedhouse.mjs uses micro bricks for every plain block. Detailed architecture, no props.

## Coins, XP, levels
- `skeleton_drop/`: `coingen.mjs` makes coin1/10/25 (pay into leaderboard `coins`, which the shops spend) from `coin25_orig.brz` (owner's hand-built coin). `gen.js` holds the per-skeleton table (rolls, drop %, brown/silver %, XP) and writes `skeleton_drop.ws`; `build.mjs` compiles it with the coins embedded. Upload the .brz files to `data/Saved/Prefabs/`.
- The chip lives in the sky at (-8260,-7400,8000) (moved 2026-10-03 evening: at road level it went missing, likely hammered; prefab loads below z 0 silently fail). Re-place with `br.Prefab.Load "skeleton_drop" -8260 -7400 8000 0 16` (only ONE copy, or XP doubles). Check: `br.Prefab.SaveRegion "chk" -8260 -7400 8000 30 30 30 0` should hold a B_1x1_Microchip.
- Keep inventory on rejoin (2026-10-03): the XP chip records leaderboard "SwordTier" (1 bronze..7 rune) when a player's coins drop by exactly a sword price (the HUD loop polls coins), and on CharacterSpawned after 30+ s unseen (a join) gives that sword back (AddInventoryItemAdv ArmingSword with the tier damage/name/colour). Only shop swords; base weapons from GetInventoryEntry can't tell tiers apart (all tiers are Weapon_ArmingSword).
- HUD: top-right `DisplayText` (text ids 52001 level, 52002 XP), redrawn on spawn, kill and /level (no loops in Wirescript).
- XP/levels are in the same chip: killer `IncLeaderboard("XP")`, Level = floor(sqrt(XP/25))+1 set with `SetLeaderboard("Level")`, status message + whisper on level-up, `/level` chat command.
- Wirescript leaderboard builtins are `GetLeaderboard` / `SetLeaderboard` / `IncLeaderboard` (also `SetTeam`, `GetTeamByName`, team leaderboard). Full builtin docs: https://wirescript.brickadia.dev/docs/builtins.md (the vendored SDK has no docs; fetch them). No broadcast-to-all builtin (ShowChatMessage is per player).
- An older Omegga `levels` plugin version is parked in `~/plugins-disabled/levels-plugin` (not loaded).
